{
  "_README": {
    "purpose": "Legacy GA4 event name -> cross-brand contract event (~/.claude/durable/ANALYTICS_CONTRACT.md).",
    "why_dual_emit": "GA4 property 538698079 (Geebs Coaching, stream G-R1VQZXY7Q1) has key events keyed to legacy names, read live from the Admin API on 2026-09-19: purchase, close_convert_lead, qualify_lead, application_submitted, apply_form_qualified_submit_attempt, calendar_booking_click, site_application_submitted, booking_started. Renaming any of them in place would silently zero a configured conversion, so the legacy leg keeps flowing untouched and the contract leg rides alongside under a DIFFERENT name.",
    "fields": {
      "event": "contract event emitted alongside the legacy name",
      "params": "static params merged into the contract leg only",
      "rename": "legacy param name -> contract param name, applied to the contract leg only",
      "mirror": "true = legacy leg only. The interaction already produced this contract event via another legacy name (or via the shared delegated layer), so emitting it again would write the same counter twice."
    }
  },
